% !! BUG FIXED ON IMPORT — the source file placed "%% VERIFY" markers INSIDE
% entries, on the same line as a field value. BibTeX has no comment syntax
% inside an entry: "%" is an ordinary character, so parsing broke at the first
% marker and every field after it was silently dropped. BibTeX reported
% "empty title / journal / year" for 8 of 18 entries and rendered them with an
% author list and nothing else. All markers are now standalone lines BETWEEN
% entries, where "%" is genuinely ignored.
%   -> The sibling project's refs.bib still has this bug. Flagged to Ting.
%
% Empty "volume = {}" / "pages = {}" fields were also removed rather than left
% blank — a missing field is silent, an empty one warns on every build.
%
% VERIFY discipline: a marker means the field was never checked against the
% source. Run the citation-audit skill before submission and delete each marker
% as it is confirmed. A marker that is not maintained is worse than none.
% ============================================================================

